WEBVTT

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.220
Ah! What a beautiful day!

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.100
Yes, what a beautiful day.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.490
Master. I'll be going now.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.560
Yes. Thank you, Martin.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.080
Oh yes!

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:21.080
Could you get me a newspaper from the
post office on your way back?

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.000
Sure.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:28.440
He's a very good worker. He's a great help.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.610
The more reason
for you to rest, Matthew.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.340
The weather is good this summer.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.840
I think we'll have a
great potato harvest.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.170
Yes.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.800
Right, I'll go get some work done.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.600
Oh, again? Why don't you rest a little?

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.180
Well now.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:04.940
The weather is great. I think
I will go and tidy the tools.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:09.680
Is that so? Whenever Anne is home,
you always have lots of plans, don't you?

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.960
No... Well now...

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:13.670
Take care.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.240
I will.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.760
It's great to see Matthew looking so lively.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.510
Anne! Help me with this, too.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.380
Yes!

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.600
Oh! Matthew...

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:48.510
Matthew!

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.130
Matthew, what's wrong with you?!

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.120
Are you feeling ill?

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.270
Matthew!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.330
Are you all right?!
Matthew! Matthew!

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.160
He has fainted.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.160
Anne, go get Martin. He's at the barn.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:09.230
Hurry up!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.540
Y-Yes!

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.440
Hang in there, Matthew!

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:20.880
Master!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.910
Martin! Come and help me!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:23.950
Y-Yes!

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.830
Hurry! Go get Dr. Spencer!
- Yes, right away!

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.330
And tell Mrs. Lynde!

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:41.900
Yes!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.930
Matthew! Matthew!

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.080
Hang in there!

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:48.930
Matthew!

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.410
What? Matthew fell down?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.970
Yes, I'm going to get the doctor now.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.020
I understand. Hurry! Go on!
- Yes.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.070
It's all right.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.510
This... This has happened many times before.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.460
I'm sure he'll recover.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:50.440
Mrs. Lynde.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:53.910
Marilla.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:07:27.990
Rachel!

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.110
Oh, Marilla.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:36.080
There's nothing we can do.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.390
Matthew! Matthew!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.920
No... Matthew can't be...

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:49.950
Yes, it's true, Anne.
I don't think I'm mistaken.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:52.540
Look at his face.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:58.710
When you've seen that look as often
as I have, you'll know what it means.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:19.250
Matthew!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.730
Matthew is dead.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:30.230
Anne looks at the still face and there
beholds the seal of the Great Presence.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.510
When the doctor arrives,

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.040
he says that Matthew died
almost instantaneously,

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.620
and probably painless.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:49.620
After examination, the doctor concludes he
must have received a sudden shock.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:56.790
The cause of the shock is found in the
newspaper Matthew had held in his hand.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:03.280
This is it! Look!
Abbey Bank has gone bankrupt!

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:06.380
Matthew must have been shocked by that.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:10.940
Marilla, this is because of what I said, isn't it?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:14.780
I knew that Abbey Bank was in trouble.
If he had listened to my advice...

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.070
Stop, Mrs. Lynde.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.030
Please. At this time...

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.330
I understand.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:25.500
I apologize for my behavior.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.040
Forgive me, Marilla!

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.600
I'm really sorry.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.570
This is difficult to say at this time,

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:47.710
but you still have a lot of things to do.
You must stay strong, Marilla.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.960
Marilla. You do understand, don't you?

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.290
What's wrong, Marilla?

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:03.390
I understand how you feel, but this isn't like you.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.900
We have to leave Marilla alone now,

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.360
so you must get a grip on yourselves.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:25.950
Anyway, Martin, take coach and go inform Mr. Bell and the Barry's.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:27.620
Yes. I'll do that.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:31.630
You have to send telegrams to the Cuthberts family.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.230
Anne, do you know them?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:39.900
When Mr. Bell and the others arrive, I'm sure everything will advance promptly.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.140
Oh, yes. You haven't put up a
mourning band on the door.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:46.540
I'm sure Marilla still has one
from when her mother died.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.520
You must get a grip on yourself.

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:55.220
The news of Matthew's passing spreads quickly throughout Avonlea,

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:01.320
and, all that day, his friends and
acquaintances come to Green Gables

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:05.990
on errands of kindness for the dead
and the bereaved family.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:10.120
Anne.

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:15.970
This was most unexpected, wasn't it?

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.780
Please let me know if you need my help.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.710
Thank you, Diana.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.820
The coffin is here, Anne.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:23.730
Y-Yes.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:31.690
Anne, bring me the white socks
and the wool cloth.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:35.010
I need to dress Matthew's body.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.740
If you don't have that, even linen would do.

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:38.970
Y-Yes.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.300
The quiet and shy Matthew Cuthbert

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:56.250
is now at the center of attention
for the first and last time.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:03.910
The white, solemn hand of Death is placed
on top of Matthew to collect him.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:12.560
Anne goes to the garden
during a lull in the busy schedule.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.260
This beautiful, old-fashioned, flower garden

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:19.540
was prepared by Matthew and Marilla's
mother when she got married.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:22.380
Even though Matthew never said it,

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:25.590
he had continuously poured
his secret love over it.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:32.220
Anne, with her anguished
tearless eyes burning in her white face,

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:36.820
picks the flowers with care,
and places them, one by one, around Matthew.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.130
If there's anything
Anne can do for Matthew,

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:45.060
this is probably the one
thing left for her to do.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:08.090
Itsuka tsuku ran
The Master's hand is there

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:16.250
Saredo mo shiuu yo
My journey may be long

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:24.710
ware inoraji
the pathways rough and steep

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:33.570
tabiji no owari no
Sufficient for each day my song

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:41.910
chikakare to wa
My way the Lord does keep

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:50.390
hi mo kurenaba
And though when evening falls

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:58.440
ishi no makura
a stone my pillow shapes

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:07.190
karine no yumenimo
The vision of our kingdom calls

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:15.470
mikuni shinoban
And here a Bethel makes

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:19.460
Amen

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.690
Matthew, you were a good fella.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:38.340
Matthew.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:23.870
Anne.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.560
I'm sorry. Can I come in?

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:40.030
Anne, would you like me to stay here tonight?

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.370
Why don't we sleep together?

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:48.140
Thank you, Diana.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:54.980
I think you won't misunderstand me
when I say I want to be alone.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.160
I'm not afraid.

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:57.940
Anne...

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:03.200
I haven't been alone one minute since it happened,

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.680
and I want to be.

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:12.530
I want to be quite silent
and quiet and try to realize it.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.670
I can't realize it.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:20.940
I never thought Matthew would die.

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:23.480
Besides the other time...
a long time ago,

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:29.980
I have never been plagued
by such an unspeakable pain.

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.010
I'm sorry, Diana.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:39.760
Diana does not quite
understand Anne.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:46.280
Marilla's impassioned grief breaks
all the bounds of natural reserve

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:50.060
and lifelong habit in its stormy rush,

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:58.060
she could comprehend better than Anne's tearless agony.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:05.980
However, the kind Diana
leaves without a word,

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:11.790
leaving Anne alone to keep her first vigil with sorrow.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:24.910
Anne hopes that the tears
will come in solitude.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:33.540
It seems to her a terrible thing that she
can not shed a tear for Matthew,

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.700
whom she has loved so much.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:42.680
Matthew, who had walked with her last evening,

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:50.300
was now lying in the dim room below,
with that awful peace on his brow.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:55.560
But still, no tears come.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:18:06.560
Instead of tears, the same horrible,
dull ache of misery keeps on tormenting Anne.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:57.460
Listen, I would never exchange
you for a dozen of them.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:04.170
Well, now. The one who got the Avery scholarship wasn't a boy, mind you,

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:06.300
but a girl.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:12.210
You're my girl. My very own girl.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.950
Anne, you're my daughter.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:20:49.870
Matthew?

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:02.890
Come, come. Be a good girl
and stop crying.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:11.430
That's enough.
Matthew can't hear you now.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:15.630
He won't come back,
no matter how much you cry.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:23.940
I know that. But today I can't stop either.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.080
Matthew was a very kind man.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:33.850
He was my irreplaceable brother.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:37.350
But this is God's will.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:41.700
Oh, Marilla. Let me cry.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:45.060
The tears don't hurt me like that ache did.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.380
Marilla.

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:55.820
Stay here for a little while with me,
and keep your arm round me, like that.

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:05.020
I couldn't have Diana stay.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:10.940
She's good and kind and sweet,
but it's not her sorrow.

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:16.590
She's outside of it, and she couldn't
come close enough to my heart to help me.

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:21.300
It's our sorrow. Yours and mine.

00:22:21.550 --> 00:22:23.030
Oh, Marilla!

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:26.100
Now that Matthew is gone, what do we do?

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:30.640
We've got each other, Anne.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:34.760
If you hadn't been here...
If you hadn't come home,

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:37.180
I don't know what I'd do.

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:40.390
Marilla...

00:22:42.330 --> 00:22:47.870
Oh, Anne, I know I've been kind of
strict and harsh with you maybe,

00:22:48.060 --> 00:22:52.760
but you mustn't think I didn't love you
as well as Matthew did, for all that.

00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:56.930
Marilla!

00:22:57.010 --> 00:23:03.230
It's never been easy for me
to say things out of my heart,

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:06.640
but at times like this it's easier.

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.620
I love you as dearly as if you
were my own flesh and blood.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:15.530
Marilla.

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:22.560
You've been my joy and comfort ever
since you came to Green Gables.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:24.160
Marilla...

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:25.600
Anne.

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.970
Next on Anne of Green Gables,
Episode 48:

00:24:07.350 --> 00:24:09.300
Matthew's Farewell

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:11.070
Please look forward to it!

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:16.840
The Adventures of Tom Sawyer

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:19.230
Taking place in the grand nature surrounding Mississippi,

00:24:19.230 --> 00:24:22.710
Tom Sawyer and his friends
experience pleasant adventures.

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:26.260
A wonderful world, full of dreams and hope.

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:29.010
The new series 'The Adventures of Tom Sawyer'

00:24:29.010 --> 00:24:30.680
will start this spring!

00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:31.920
Please look forward to it!
